CAT = "s24Accounts"; SEG = "ACC"
Q = [
('Under the Customer Identification Program rule for broker-dealers, the records used to verify a customer\'s identity must be kept for:',
 'Five years after the account is closed', ['Three years after the account is opened', 'Six years after the last trade', 'One year after the account is closed'],
 'The CIP rule (31 CFR 1023.220) requires identifying information to be kept for five years after the account is closed, and records of verification methods for five years after they are made.'),
('When a legal entity customer opens an account, the beneficial ownership rule requires the firm to identify each individual who owns at least:',
 '25% of the entity, plus one person who controls it', ['10% of the entity, plus every director', '50% of the entity, plus the auditor', '5% of the entity, plus each officer'],
 'The customer due diligence rule (31 CFR 1010.230) requires identifying and verifying each individual owning 25 percent or more of the equity interests and one individual with significant responsibility to control the entity.'),
('A firm files a suspicious activity report on a customer. The customer later asks whether a report was filed. The firm:',
 'May not reveal that a SAR was filed', ['Must tell the customer within 30 days', 'May tell the customer once the SAR is accepted', 'Must ask FINRA before answering'],
 'The Bank Secrecy Act rules (31 CFR 1023.320(e)) make SARs confidential: a broker-dealer may not disclose a SAR or information that would reveal its existence to the person involved.'),
('A customer brings in $6,000 in cash in the morning and $5,500 in cash that afternoon to fund her account. The firm must:',
 'File a Currency Transaction Report, since the day\'s cash exceeds $10,000', ['Do nothing, since each deposit is under $10,000', 'File a SAR only, since a CTR needs one deposit', 'Refuse the second deposit until the next day'],
 'Currency transactions by or for the same person in one business day are added together. Cash of more than $10,000 in a day requires a Currency Transaction Report to FinCEN, due within 15 days.'),
('A new account holder\'s name matches an entry on OFAC\'s Specially Designated Nationals list, and the match is confirmed. The firm must:',
 'Block the property and report it to OFAC', ['Close the account and return the money', 'Ask the customer to explain the match', 'Report it only in the next FOCUS filing'],
 'U.S. persons must block property of persons on the SDN list and report blocked property to OFAC within 10 business days, rather than return the assets.'),
('After receiving a FinCEN Section 314(a) request, a broker-dealer must search its records and report any matches within:',
 '14 days', ['24 hours', '30 days', '90 days'],
 'Under 31 CFR 1010.520, a financial institution receiving a 314(a) request must search its records and report any match to FinCEN within 14 days, and keep the request confidential.'),
('A firm that carries customer accounts must have its anti-money laundering program independently tested at least:',
 'Once each calendar year', ['Once every three years', 'Only after FINRA finds a problem', 'Once every five years'],
 'Rule 3310(c) requires annual independent testing, on a calendar-year basis, for most members; a member that does not execute transactions for customers or hold customer accounts may test every two years.'),
('For a funds transfer of $3,000 or more, the Bank Secrecy Act\'s recordkeeping and travel rules require the firm to:',
 'Keep the transfer details and pass them to the next institution', ['Get FinCEN\'s approval before sending it', 'File a Currency Transaction Report on it', 'Hold the funds for three business days'],
 'For transmittals of funds of $3,000 or more, 31 CFR 1010.410 requires records of the transfer and the travel rule requires the transmitting institution to pass key information along with it.'),
('Under Regulation S-P as amended in 2024, a firm whose customers\' sensitive information was accessed without authorization must notify affected individuals:',
 'As soon as practicable, and no later than 30 days after learning of it', ['Within 24 hours of learning of it', 'Only if a customer reports a loss', 'Within one year of the incident'],
 'The 2024 amendments to Regulation S-P (Rule 248.30) require an incident response program and notice to affected individuals as soon as practicable, but not later than 30 days after the firm becomes aware of the incident.'),
('Under amended Regulation S-P, a firm\'s service providers must notify the firm of a breach affecting its customer information within:',
 '72 hours', ['24 hours', '10 business days', '30 days'],
 'The 2024 amendments require firms to oversee service providers through policies requiring them to notify the firm as soon as possible, and no later than 72 hours after becoming aware of a breach.'),
('Regulation S-ID requires a broker-dealer that offers covered accounts to have a written identity theft program that:',
 'Detects and responds to red flags and is approved by the board or senior management', ['Is filed with and approved by FINRA staff', 'Covers only accounts over $100,000', 'Is reviewed by customers each year'],
 'Regulation S-ID (17 CFR 248.201) requires a written program to identify, detect and respond to red flags of identity theft, with initial approval by the board or a designated senior manager and periodic updates.'),
('A new customer declines to give the name of a trusted contact person. Under Rule 4512 the firm:',
 'May still open the account', ['Must refuse to open the account', 'Must name a family member itself', 'Must restrict the account to cash only'],
 'Rule 4512 requires a reasonable effort to obtain a trusted contact person for a non-institutional account, but an account can be opened and kept if the customer does not provide one.'),
('A customer asks the firm to hold her mail while she travels. Under Rule 3150 the firm may do so if it:',
 'Has her written instructions stating how long to hold it', ['Gets FINRA\'s approval for the hold', 'Holds it for no longer than 10 days', 'Sends it to her representative instead'],
 'Rule 3150 allows holding mail on the customer\'s written instructions specifying the time period, with the firm telling the customer of other ways to get account information and verifying the instructions at reasonable intervals.'),
('For an account opened for a corporation, Rule 4512 requires the firm to keep a record of:',
 'The names of the persons authorized to transact for the account', ['The corporation\'s last five tax returns', 'The home addresses of all shareholders', 'The corporation\'s credit rating'],
 'Rule 4512(a)(3) requires, for an account of a legal entity, the names of any persons authorized to transact business on its behalf.'),
('SEC Rule 17a-3 requires a firm to send each customer a copy of the account record for review at least every:',
 '36 months', ['12 months', '24 months', '60 months'],
 'Rule 17a-3(a)(17) requires the account record to be furnished within 30 days of opening and at intervals of no more than 36 months, and within 30 days after a change of name, address or investment objective.'),
('Under Rule 2165, a firm may place a temporary hold on a disbursement from a specified adult\'s account when it reasonably believes:',
 'Financial exploitation has occurred, is occurring or will be attempted', ['The customer\'s investments have lost value', 'The customer has changed her address twice', 'The customer has asked for a large check'],
 'Rule 2165 lets a firm hold disbursements of funds or securities, and since 2022 securities transactions, for a specified adult (65 and older, or 18 and older with an impairment) when it reasonably believes financial exploitation is involved.'),
]
